            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Personal Struggles and Expressiveness</strong><br>\nThroughout his life, Goya faced many personal struggles, including his health issues and witnessing the societal effects of war. These experiences deeply influenced his turn towards a more personal and expressive style in his art.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Last Years in Bordeaux</strong><br>\nIn his final years, Goya lived in self-imposed exile in Bordeaux, France, due to political unrest in Spain. There, he continued to paint and experiment with lithography, producing more innovative works.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Legacy and Influence on Modern Art</strong><br>\nGoya died in 1828, leaving a legacy that cemented him as a forerunner of modern art. His bold techniques and the emotional power of his work continue to influence artists and remain relevant today.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
